---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { projects } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Workbench — Javier Ponz" description="Projects, repositories and shipped work by Javier Ponz, with scope and status stated plainly."><section class="hero"><p class="kicker">Workbench</p><h1>Things I am <span class="serif">making</span>.</h1><p class="lede">Every project here has source code you can read, a stated scope, and a status that matches reality. Two of them are running in production.</p></section><section class="grid"><span class="label">Projects</span><div class="cards">{projects.map((project)=><a class="card" href={project.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span class="meta">{project.status} · {project.kind}</span><h3>{project.title} ↗</h3><p>{project.description}</p></a>)}</div></section><section class="grid"><span class="label">Deep dive</span><div class="copy"><h2>How one of them got shipped.</h2><p>Memento Mori went from an idea to a live deployment with release gates, cross-platform CI and an immutable-image rollback path. <a href="/memento-mori">Read the case study →</a></p></div></section><section class="grid"><span class="label">Scope note</span><div class="notice">These are personal projects and learning artefacts, built and maintained by me. They are not client deliverables.</div></section></Layout>
